## Audit — paths that can run an over-limit model on one card

- `scripts/stress-release.sh:59-62` + `:86` — `ENVS` copied verbatim from the newest app log's ` env: ` line, then `ENVS+=("GGML_METAL_DEVICE_LIST=${GGML_METAL_DEVICE_LIST:-0,1}")`. If that log carries `GGML_METAL_DEVICE_INDEX=0` (or caller sets it), the run gets `-ngl 99` (`:79`) with one card and any model passed at `:30` — no size check. Real risk; needs the same stat-vs-limit guard or a stripped `GGML_METAL_DEVICE_INDEX`.
- `scripts/tp-baseline.sh:53` — `run solo GGML_METAL_DEVICE_LIST=1 -- -sm none` on `$MODEL` (GLM-4-9B-0414-Q4_K_M, absent here; nominal ~5.5-5.8 GB, near the 5.905 GB line). Hard-coded single die, no size check.
- `scripts/tp-baseline.sh:109-110` — `spec_solo_none` / `spec_solo_ngram` use `GGML_METAL_DEVICE_LIST=1 -- -sm none` with `SPEC_MODEL` unset, i.e. `$MODEL`. Same pattern. (`spec_qwen_*` rows at `:131-134` are TP4, and the comment at `:122-124` documents that solo 35B was dropped for exactly this reason.)
- Nothing else: `tools/ab.sh:56,110,181` use `-sm tensor`/`layer`/`row` with no card pinning (all devices); `SMOKE_MODEL` defaults to the 0.6B (`:28`). `scripts/mgpu-report.sh:19,55`, `mgpu-server-check.sh:38`, `test-wave64-fa.sh:46`, `test-spec-decode.sh:44`, `spec-kernel-bench.py:96,112` and `make-engine-zip.sh:98` (generated `start.sh`) pin no card. `scripts/check-kernel-coverage.sh:29` pins a card but runs `test-backend-ops`, no model.
- `tp-baseline.sh` targets the 4×W6800X box, not this Mac Pro; its GLM and Qwen models are not in `/Users/sam/models`.

